# Datagrams on port 47808 that are not well-formed BACnet/IP. None may
# panic. A length field that disagrees with the datagram is kept, not
# refused, so the sender can be found.

81 0a => error truncated 4/2
82 0a 00 04 => error not-bacnet-ip 130
00 => error truncated 4/1
45 00 00 1c => error not-bacnet-ip 69
81 00 00 05 00 => error wrong-length 0/1
81 00 00 08 00 00 00 00 => error wrong-length 0/4
81 05 00 07 00 3c 00 => error wrong-length 5/3
81 04 00 08 c0 a8 01 0a => error wrong-length 4/4
81 01 00 0d c0 a8 01 01 ba c0 ff ff ff => error wrong-length 1/9
81 07 00 0f 0a 00 00 05 ba c0 00 3c 00 5a 00 => error wrong-length 7/11
81 02 00 05 00 => error wrong-length 2/1
81 08 00 0b 0a 00 00 05 ba c0 00 => error wrong-length 8/7
# The length field says 32; the datagram is 8.
81 0a 00 20 01 00 10 08 => original-unicast npdu 01001008 (length 32, datagram 8)
# The length field says 4; the datagram carries more.
81 0b 00 04 01 00 10 08 => original-broadcast npdu 01001008 (length 4, datagram 8)
